{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"courageous-deserving-manatee","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nDiscovered while landing abasic-doddering-harrier (annotate the attest package for the typing ratchet). Annotating 12 `repo_root` parameters pushed four function signatures past the line-length limit, so `ruff format` wrapped them onto multiple lines. `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` went from **784 to 793 LOC** against the hard 800 cap in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`.\n\nThe harrier change itself PASSES the module-size gate (793 < 800) and is correct as landed — this ticket is NOT a defect in it. But the file now has **7 lines of headroom**, which is effectively zero: the next routine edit (one new helper, one more wrapped signature, one added docstring line) trips the CI module-size gate and blocks an unrelated change with a failure that has nothing to do with its author's work.\n\nThis is the same near-cap class of finding the parent epic (broke-boarish-hagfish) is already draining for structured_run.py, compact.py, and event_append.py — authorship.py simply was not in the audit's near-cap set when the epic was scoped, because at 784 it sat just under the threshold and the typing work is what consumed the remaining margin.\n\n## Why a split rather than re-wrapping\nReverting the wrapping is not available: the wrapping is `ruff format` output and `make lint` runs `ruff format --check`, so the formatter's layout is the enforced one. The headroom has to come from removing code, not from reflowing it.\n\n## Plan\n- Split `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` along an EXISTING call-graph seam, per the AGENTS.md module-size policy (split only at seams that already exist; never mechanically to hit a number; never create a file < 100 LOC).\n- The obvious seam is the **git-ancestry/commit-resolution layer** — a cluster that already calls only into itself and `subprocess`, and is consumed by the verify layer through a narrow interface: `resolve_event_commit`, `resolve_position_commit`, `build_ticket_position_commit_map`, `build_introducing_commit_map`, `build_position_commit_map` (~330 LOC together, comfortably over the 100 LOC floor). The verification layer (`verify_authorship*`, `identify_signer`, `keys_valid_at_anchor`) stays put.\n- **Preserve public import paths** by re-exporting the moved symbols from `authorship`, so the split is behavior-identical. This matters more than usual here: tests reference these as `authorship.resolve_event_commit` (tests/unit/test_authorship_batched_ticket_map_7084.py, test_identity_ts2_09f9_heldout.py, test_authorship_resolver_git_flags.py, test_identity_perf_1cc0.py) and at least one monkeypatches through that attribute, so the module attribute must keep resolving.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `wc -l src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` reports a value that leaves real headroom under the 800 cap (target <= 500 per the AGENTS.md 200-500 target band).\n- [ ] Every new module created by the split is >= 100 LOC.\n- [ ] Public import paths preserved: `python -c 'from rebar.attest import authorship; [getattr(authorship, n) for n in (\"resolve_event_commit\",\"resolve_position_commit\",\"build_ticket_position_commit_map\",\"build_introducing_commit_map\",\"build_position_commit_map\")]'` exits 0.\n- [ ] `mypy src/rebar/attest --disallow-untyped-defs` still reports no errors (the harrier invariant is not regressed by the split), and the Any-count grep over `src/rebar/attest/*.py` still reports exactly 2.\n- [ ] make lint, make typecheck, and the CI pytest lane are green; no behavior change (annotations/imports only — no logic edits).\n\n## Non-overlap\nTouches `src/rebar/attest/authorship.py` plus new sibling module(s) in the same package. Must land AFTER abasic-doddering-harrier (which is what creates the 793-line state).","id":"760f-608f-4c69-449a","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Split authorship.py: 793/800 LOC, 7 lines of module-size headroom"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786597447143591001,"uuid":"993e9feb-c376-41cc-897c-08e9ec5926af"}